  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">EU Support to Floods Recovery in Bosnia and Herzegovina</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">EU Support to Flood Recovery in Bosnia and Herzegovina is an EU-funded intervention, designed to provide an immediate response to the needs of the population in local communities in BiH directly affected by the natural disaster declared in October 2024. The project will operate in 8 local governments in BiH (Konjic, Kiseljak, Fojnica, Mostar, Kre&#x161;evo, Vare&#x161;, and Drvar) in helping them effectively and sustainably recover from the event, especially focusing on socially and economically vulnerable</narrative>
  </description>
